From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve original HBM task capacity with native payload and MEM layouts
Upstream-base: 132cdee912111da6c9973b1dce13651f1979b07d
Classification: native LP64 storage/header ABI and modern compiler compatibility only.

Retain all original nested SoundArchivePlayer task declarations and methods.
Reflect their actual sizeof/alignof and the real MEM headers so the native
unit heap preserves TASK_NUM128 and fits every source task. Keep the original
32-byte static alignment with a compile-time compatibility check. Read the
native unit header's named blockSize; keep the console area,64-byte request
and raw header-offset expression exact. Task IDs,priorities,allocation retry,
execution,cancellation and recycle algorithms remain unchanged.

Use legal placement-new/dependent-type/pure-destructor/constant-expression
syntax and precise native owning includes without changing fields or bodies.
Native u32 aliases unsigned int: exclude duplicated identical Start/Hold/
Prepare wrappers and the independently uncalled LoadGroup unsigned-int inline.
The latter's original self-recursive body remains exact in the console branch;
canonical implementation and actual int-id/label call bindings stay unchanged.
No SoundArchivePlayer loading,HBM initialization or source readiness is added.

